#. Diagram label
msgid "Review the draft publication"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/collab/processes/content/draft-to-publication.bpmn:112
#. Diagram label
msgid "Run publication QA gates"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/collab/processes/content/draft-to-publication.bpmn:81
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Runs in parallel with Lane_ReviewTeam (Gateway_ReviewJoin waits on both) but does not own the approve/reject gateway that follows: sign-off here is needed for the join to complete, and nothing more."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/collab/processes/content/draft-to-publication.bpmn:77
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Runs in parallel with the review team and the SMEs when a draft goes out for PUBLIC comment: the circulated draft is the frozen, line-numbered review version, and every comment that comes back is placed, triaged, weighed and decided in Process_PublicComment. Like Lane_Sme it feeds the join and does not own the approve/reject gateway; an accepted comment reaches the document through its own change set, not through this gateway."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/collab/processes/content/draft-to-publication.bpmn:85
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Sits between review's approval and the publish: a second gate on an approved draft, answering whether the release is authorised to ship."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/collab/processes/content/draft-to-publication.bpmn:255
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Someone else holds the bean; this run stops without touching it."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/collab/processes/content/draft-to-publication.bpmn:141
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The draft publication is circulated to the review team for formal review."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/collab/processes/content/draft-to-publication.bpmn:131
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The editing sub-process. Every change to the corpus goes through its HCI validation gate — a red draft is fixed there, never by patching the built artifact."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/collab/processes/content/draft-to-publication.bpmn:216
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Version bump, release notes, tag, build the final artifacts, deploy to the publication platform. The deploy is the general render-kg-to-cdn step with the RELEASE root as its publication root URL — the same step a staging preview takes with a root under it; the target (GitHub Pages, or a folio's own platform) is chosen by its Tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/collab/processes/content/draft-to-publication.bpmn:215
#. Diagram label
msgid "Version, tag and publish"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/collab/processes/content/draft-to-publication.bpmn:228
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "What shipped is resolved; what slipped stays open and carries into the next cycle."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/collab/processes/content/draft-to-publication.bpmn:156
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "When the draft goes out for public comment: the release date is agreed, the draft is frozen as a line-numbered public comment release, every channel is set up against it and announced, and the comments that come back are placed, triaged, recommended on by the review committee and decided by the editor (Process_PublicCommentRelease, which calls Process_PublicComment)."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/collab/processes/content/draft-to-publication.bpmn:46
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Where both rejection paths loop back to: a red QA gate directly, and a review rejection once each finding has become a bean."
msgstr ""

